{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-hydration restricted to the rows a caller already knows changed."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"store"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ids","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"deleted"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"text":"> = [], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","text":"MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"store","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The live store to reconcile."}]}]},{"name":"ids","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The identities to re-read. IDs matching no row, and IDs"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"belonging to another entity type, are harmless."}]}]},{"name":"deleted","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Identities known to have been deleted elsewhere.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The O(k) counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"text":", which re-reads every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of every registered entity on every tick. Where a sync signal carries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"text":" identities changed, this spends that knowledge: one batched fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per 500 IDs instead of a full-table scan, and only the named entities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconciled. Everything else in state is left exactly as it was.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every guarantee "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes holds here. Pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes are flushed first; an ID with unflushed local intent — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drained-but-unflushed write, an un-drained edit, a pending deletion, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write whose save failed, or an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","isActive":true},{"text":" hold — always wins, and that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not configurable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A partial read cannot tell a deleted row from one that was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never asked about, so this ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" infers a deletion. An ID vanishes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only if you name it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleted"},{"text":", and only if the resolved policy grants","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/removesMissingEntities","isActive":true},{"text":". Name only what you have positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"evidence for — a history tombstone, not an empty fetch. In exchange,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there is no empty-snapshot guard to work around: this can remove the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"last surviving entity, which "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" cannot."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID named in "},{"code":"deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that storage ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"still holds","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is not removed. A live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is evidence the deletion was itself undone elsewhere; a tombstone can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be stale.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Deferred-rows-are-re-offered","level":2,"text":"Deferred rows are re-offered","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tick may read a row and decline to apply it — an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hold is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exemption that leaves no other trace. Those rows are remembered by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity and re-offered on the next call, on top of whatever ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ids"},{"text":" names,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"so a caller does not have to re-queue them against its own signal. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matters here because a sync signal is generally not resent and releasing a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"hold writes no transaction of its own, so without it a hold would quietly"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"become a veto. A call whose read throws is remembered the same way: the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"identities it was handed are owed, not dropped with the read.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"text":" shares the same debt, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"either path settles what the other deferred. Both discard it when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container is swapped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registered "},{"code":"collapse:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolvers do not run here — a resolver is handed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole table and asked which rows survive, and a subset would have it","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"judge a world it cannot see. Duplicate rows are still collapsed on read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and still reported. Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/collapseDuplicates(into:)-7d2no","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or a full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to reclaim them."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergeremote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"role":"symbol","title":"mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeRemote"},{"k